.\" Manpage for navune.
.TH NAVUNE 1 "2026-09-17" "navune" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
navune \- measure the structural quality of a codebase
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B navune
.B analyze
.RI [ path ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B navune
.B init
.RI [ path ]
.br
.B navune
.B version
.br
.B navune
.B help
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B navune
computes structural quality metrics for Go, TypeScript/JavaScript, Python, C,
and C++ codebases: physical and logical SLOC, cyclomatic and cognitive
complexity, comment density, function shape, duplication, internal dependency
graphs, cyclic dependencies, and Martin's coupling metrics. It evaluates the
result against configurable budgets, reports deterministic structural smells,
and emits a transparent 0\-100 composite score.
.PP
The unit of analysis is the file. Test files are analyzed but reported in a
separate
.I tests
namespace and excluded from budgets, cycles, coupling, the composite, and the
smell layer. Only imports that resolve to an analyzed file become graph edges;
unresolved imports (standard library, node_modules, site\-packages, system
headers) never do.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B analyze
.RI [ path ]
Measure the codebase rooted at
.I path
(default
.BR . ).
Writes a report to standard output unless
.B \-\-out
is given.
.TP
.B init
.RI [ path ]
Write a commented
.B navune.yaml
template into the directory
.I path
(default
.BR . ).
Fails if the file already exists.
.TP
.B version
Print the version, platform, and supported languages.
.B \-V
and
.B \-\-version
are aliases.
.TP
.B help
.RI [ command ]
Show top\-level help, or help for
.IR command .
.B \-h
and
.B \-\-help
are aliases.
.SH OPTIONS
Global options:
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.PP
Options for
.BR "navune analyze" :
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Use
.I FILE
instead of discovering
.B navune.yaml
by walking upward from the analyzed path.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " FMT"
Report format:
.BR text " (default), " json ", or " mermaid .
.TP
.BI \-\-out " FILE"
Write the report to
.I FILE
instead of standard output.
.TP
.BR \-\-verbose ", " \-v
Add per\-function detail: a
.I functions_detail
array per file in JSON, and functions carrying smells in the text report.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help for
.B analyze
and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Pass: all error\-tier budgets satisfied.
.TP
.B 1
Breach: at least one error\-tier budget was exceeded.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or configuration error.
.TP
.B 3
Internal error (for example, a source file could not be parsed).
.PP
Warn\-tier breaches are reported but do not change the exit code.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I navune.yaml
Project configuration: exclusions, budgets, weights, smell rules,
per\-language overrides, and C/C++ include paths. Discovered by walking upward
from the analyzed path, or selected explicitly with
.BR \-\-config .
.TP
.I navune.yaml.example
Sample configuration shipped in the source distribution.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B navune analyze .
Analyze the current directory and print the text report.
.TP
.B navune analyze ./src \-\-format json
Emit the versioned JSON report.
.TP
.B navune analyze . \-\-format mermaid \-\-out deps.mmd
Write the dependency graph, with cycles grouped into subgraphs.
.TP
.B navune init
Scaffold a commented
.B navune.yaml
in the current directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.I docs/usage.md
in the navune source distribution for the full CLI reference,
.I docs/metrics.md
for metric definitions, and
.I docs/adr/
for the design record.
